// KR-69, the negated position. `!OS_WINODWS` is activatable by every target there is — the gate is
// satisfiable, so "must be activatable" alone would let it through — and it is the SAME typo, keeping
// the declaration on every build instead of dropping it on all but one. The rule is therefore about
// the NAME a known target can produce, not about whether the gate can be satisfied, and it is applied
// wherever the name appears.
@compileFor(!OS_WINODWS)
fn int32 everywhereButWindows() { return 3; }

fn int32 main() { return everywhereButWindows() - 3; }
